# Primitive aliases on mutable and immutable bindings

Verifies primitive and nullable aliases annotate both mutable `let` bindings
and immutable `const` bindings without changing their concrete values.

>>> source
type Count = int
type Label = string
type Switch = bool
type OptionalLabel = Label?

let count: Count = 1
count = 2
const label: Label = "ready"
const enabled: Switch = true
const missing: OptionalLabel = null

print(count)
print(label)
print(enabled)
print(missing == null)

<<< stdout
2
ready
true
true

<<< stderr
